# ── the published site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Output, not source. Republish writes every one of these files from the
# plugin and the database, so nothing here is authored and nothing here is
# lost by not tracking it.
#
# It was tracked until now, and the churn is why it stopped being: a single
# republish moves twenty-six files whose only difference is a cache-bust
# stamp, and merging two branches that had each republished meant resolving
# twenty-seven conflicts that contained no content change at all.
#
# The trade is deliberate and worth stating plainly, because it is easy to
# discover later and mistake for an oversight: THE REPOSITORY IS NO LONGER A
# RECORD OF WHAT IS DEPLOYED. To know what the live site is serving, look at
# the live site. The recovery route is the content export, which holds the
# settings and the vehicles, plus Republish to rebuild the files from them —
# see the backups section below, which is the other half of this.
frontend/

# ── backups ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Snapshots of the published site, taken by hand before risky work. They are
# copies of frontend/ and belong on disk, not in the history.
frontend.bak-*/
*.bak
*.bak-*
vesla-landing.php.bak*

# Settings exports and the automatic snapshots the plugin writes. These hold
# every word of the site's content and, in the contact section, the address
# enquiries are sent to — they are a recovery route, not source.
vesla-settings-*.json
content-2*.json
vesla-backups/

# ── local WordPress ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The plugin here is the source. The WordPress install it runs inside is not:
# it carries wp-config.php, the database credentials and the uploads folder.
wp-config.php
wp-content/uploads/
*.sql
*.sqlite

# ── the machine, not the project ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code's own working area: session scratch, and the extra
# checkouts it makes under .claude/worktrees. Generated, and specific to
# this machine.
.claude/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# ── editor and OS leftovers ───────────────────────────────────────────────
*~
*.swp
*.swo
*.tmp
.~lock.*
